{number: 45}
{title: Jesus Paid It All}
{key: Eb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Eb] I hear the Savior say,
"Thy strength indeed is [Bb7] small;
Child of [Eb] weakness, watch and [Ab] pray,
Find in [Eb] Me thine [Bb7] all in [Eb] all."
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Eb] Jesus paid it [Cm] all,
[Eb] All to Him I [Bb] owe;
[Eb] Sin had left a [Ab] crimson stain,
He [Eb] washed it [Bb7] white as [Eb] snow.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Eb] Lord, now indeed I find
Thy pow'r, and Thine a-[Bb7] lone,
Can [Eb] change the leper's [Ab] spots
And [Eb] melt the [Bb7] heart of [Eb] stone.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Eb] For nothing good have I
Whereby Thy grace to [Bb7] claim;
I'll [Eb] wash my garments [Ab] white
In the [Eb] blood of [Bb7] Calv'ry's [Eb] Lamb.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
And [Eb] when before the throne
I stand in Him com-[Bb7] plete,
"Jesus [Eb] died my soul to [Ab] save,"
My [Eb] lips shall [Bb7] still re-[Eb] peat.
